# q79 Bulk-to-Boundary Dirac Family Functor and Boundary-Source Cutset Theorem

## 1. Claim boundary

This theorem closes two previously separate questions under `B.QFT.02`.

First, once a physical moving-boundary package is supplied, the selected q79
bulk Dirac operator canonically produces the tangential Dirac family, its APS
projectors and its BFV Green form. Arbitrary finite operator entries are not
additional source data.

Second, the earlier finite crossing

\[
A(t)=\operatorname{diag}(-2,t,3)
\]

is the endpoint of an explicit spectral-flow-preserving homotopy from a
three-mode Galerkin restriction of a continuum Dirac operator on the shared
circle.

The theorem does **not** select the physical moving boundary, connection
history, endpoint comparison or full Dai--Freed phase.

